# List View Pattern

Reuse the existing list-view stack. Do not recreate schema, APIs, or `ListViewModal`.

- Model: `SavedListView` (`entityType`, `columns` JSON, `filters` JSON, `userId`, `isDefault`)
- APIs: `GET/POST /api/admin/list-views`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/admin/list-views/[id]`
- UI: `src/components/ListViewModal.tsx`
- Sorting helpers: `sortItems`, `nextSortConfig`, `SortConfig` from `@/lib/sort-utils`

Copy the integration in `src/app/admin/patrons/page.tsx`.

## New list page checklist

1. Define `availableColumns` as `{ id, label }[]` for that entity
2. Fetch views with `entityType` matching the entity name (`patron`, `turnout`, …)
3. Auto-select the user's default view on first load
4. Header: "Create List View" (`sf-btn-secondary`) + "Add" link (`sf-btn-primary`)
5. Toolbar: view `<select>`, delete-selected-view control, search input (`sf-input`)
6. Apply saved-view filters, then search, then `sortItems`
7. Render only `selectedView.columns` (or all `availableColumns` if no view)
8. Render `ListViewModal` with `entityType`, `availableColumns`, `onSave`, optional `existingView`

## Filter operators

`equals`, `not_equals`, `contains`, `not_contains`, `greater_than`, `less_than`, `greater_equal`, `less_equal` — compare case-insensitively for strings.

## API / audit

- `authenticateRequest`; views are scoped to `user.userId`
- Mutations: `setCurrentUserId` / `clearCurrentUserId` (including on error)
- POST requires `name`, `entityType`, and `columns`
